---- what it is for
of a class, FORWARDREF => {'x': ForwardRef('NotThere[int]', is_class=True, owner=<class '__main__.C'>), 'y': <class 'int'>, 'z': 'a string', 'w': list[ForwardRef('AlsoNot.attribute', is_class=True, owner=<class '__main__.C'>)]}
of a function, FORWARDREF => {'a': ForwardRef('Nowhere', owner=<function function at ADDRESS>), 'b': <class 'int'>, 'return': ForwardRef('Nothing | None', owner=<function function at ADDRESS>)}
of a class, STRING => {'x': 'NotThere[int]', 'y': 'int', 'z': 'a string', 'w': 'list[AlsoNot.attribute]'}
of a function, STRING => {'a': 'Nowhere', 'b': 'int', 'return': 'Nothing | None'}
of a class, VALUE => NameError: name 'NotThere' is not defined
of a function, VALUE => NameError: name 'Nowhere' is not defined
a dataclass => (D(a=1, b=1, c=2), [('a', ForwardRef('Undefined', is_class=True, owner=<class '__main__.D'>)), ('b', <class 'int'>), ('c', 'ClassVar[int]')], None)
